# ---- data (1 GB+ scenes, model weights - regeneratable) ----
# everything under data/ is regeneratable EXCEPT the curated demo upload
# set (data/demo_upload/), the three baked demo scenes + registry, and the
# lightweight ISRO TMC reference library (browse PNGs + PDS4 labels only -
# never the DTM rasters), which are committed so a fresh Render/Vercel
# clone is demo-ready with multi-instrument auto-selection working.
data/*
!data/demo_upload/
!data/demo_upload/**
!data/processed/
data/processed/*
!data/processed/ohrc_real/
!data/processed/ohrc_real/**
!data/processed/tycho_synthetic/
!data/processed/tycho_synthetic/**
!data/processed/demo_tmc/
!data/processed/demo_tmc/**
!data/processed/registry.json
!data/reference/
data/reference/lro_nac/*
!data/reference/tmc/
!data/reference/tmc/**
data/reference/tmc/_scanning/
!data/reference/iirs/
!data/reference/iirs/**
backend/models/*.onnx
*.onnx
!backend/models/descriptor.onnx
Unconfirmed*.crdownload
*.zip
!data/demo_upload/product_pds4_demo.zip

# ---- secrets ----
.env
backend/.env
frontend/.env
_test_integrations.py


# ---- python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# ---- node/vercel ----
node_modules/
.vercel/

# ---- extracted big rasters (layer caches - re-extractable) ----
data/reference/tmc/*/dtm.tif
data/reference/tmc/*/dtm.tif.part
data/reference/iirs/*/cube.qub
data/reference/iirs/*/cube.qub.part

# ---- local raw archives (never commit; live on Kaggle Drive datasets) ----
/ch2_*.tar
/ch2_iir_*.zip
backend/models/*.onnx.bak
!data/processed/tmc2_metric_demo/
!data/processed/tmc2_metric_demo/**
!data/processed/iirs_mineral_demo/
!data/processed/iirs_mineral_demo/**

# ---- layer result caches ARE committed (tiny, ~880 KB total) so a fresh
# Render clone serves the FULL 5-layer experience with zero big rasters:
#   data/reference/tmc/*/metric_dem.npy  (192^2 metric heights/product)
#   data/reference/iirs/*/minerals.npz   (classified mineral maps)
# layers.py is cache-first: these short-circuit before any dtm.tif /
# cube.qub access, so the multi-GB rasters never need to exist.
kaggle.json
backend/kaggle.json
!data/processed/ohrc_polar_20211222/`n!data/processed/ohrc_polar_20211222/**
